nian"}, "word": "înflăcăra"}, {"language": {"code": "ru", "name": "Russian"}, "word": "пыла́ть"}, {"language": {"code": "es", "name": "Spanish"}, "word": "flamear"}, {"language": {"code": "sv", "name": "Swedish"}, "word": "flamma"}, {"language": {"code": "sv", "name": "Swedish"}, "word": "flamma upp"}], "subsenses": []}, {"definition": "To burst forth like flame; to break out in violence of passion; to be kindled with zeal or ardour.", "tags": [], "examples": [], "quotes": [{"text": "He flamed with indignation.", "reference": "1849–1861, Thomas Babington Macaulay, chapter II, in The History of England from the Accession of James the Second, volume (please specify |volume=I to V), London: Longman, Brown, Green, and Longmans, →OCLC:"}], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [{"language": {"code": "bg", "name": "Bulgarian"}, "word": "пламвам"}, {"language": {"code": "bg", "name": "Bulgarian"}, "word": "пламна"}, {"language": {"code": "bg", "name": "Bulgarian"}, "word": "пламтя"}, {"language": {"code": "bg", "name": "Bulgarian"}, "word": "паля се"}, {"language": {"code": "fi", "name": "Finnish"}, "word": "leimahtaa"}], "subsenses": []}, {"definition": "(Internet, ambitransitive) To post a destructively critical or abusive message (to somebody).", "tags": ["Internet", "ambitransitive"], "examples": ["I flamed him for spamming in my favourite newsgroup."], "quotes": [{"text": "I wish you had the nerve to put your own name on that article, rather than logging into a public account to do it. I would have prefered^([sic]) to respond to you personally, rather than burden the net with my flaming, particularly since opinions like yours are best left ignored. But I feel I must respond to this one.", "reference": "1983 October 20, Joe Ziegler, net.motss (Usenet):"}, {"text": "This was one of the highest points of the show for me. Playin' followed, with a nice jam afterwards. After that, Jerry wandered into Crazy Fingers. (I had been hoping for Terrapin...oh well. Crazy 